Title: Businesses call for Channel Island collaboration, survey finds
Date: 2025-07-14
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [{'Speaker': 'Alex Ruddy, IoD Jersey Chair', 'Text': 'the survey provided a "clear mandate for action".', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 5, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 47}}, {'Speaker': 'Alex Ruddy, IoD Jersey Chair', 'Text': 'While our members are confident in their own organisations, they are calling for bold, strategic investment and policy clarity to restore wider economic confidence.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 6, 'StartChar': 11, 'EndChar': 146}}, {'Speaker': 'Alex Ruddy, IoD Jersey Chair', 'Text': "Collaboration across the Channel Islands, support for innovation, and a focus on infrastructure and housing are essential to Jersey's future prosperity.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 7, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 128}}, {'Speaker': "Richard Hemans, IoD Guernsey's lead on economics", 'Text': 'There is clear recognition from the business community in both islands that - given the same challenges apply to both islands and our economic, geographical, demographic, constitutional and fiscal profile is so similar - the best way to confront our mutual challenges is to work together more closely.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 14, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 317}}], 'Description': [{'Description': 'The Institute of Directors (IoD) Jersey released findings from its second economic confidence survey following input from 70 members.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 2, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 102}}, {'Description': "The findings suggest 56% of respondents were optimistic about their own organisations but only 17% were optimistic about Jersey's overall economy. Top priorities for growth in Jersey included infrastructure investment, attracting new industries and housing affordability.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 3, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 220}}, {'Description': "Responses found both islands faced similar economic challenges following the findings of Guernsey IOD's own survey published at the end of June, and urged political leaders to work together.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 4, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 168}}, {'Description': 'Jersey respondents said they wanted to work with Guernsey for its fiscal deficit strategies by reducing public spending and driving economic growth.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 9, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 119}}, {'Description': 'Survey results found entrepreneurship and innovation could be supported through tax incentives, youth talent attraction and skills development.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 10, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 128}}, {'Description': 'It also found AI adoption was in its early stages with 70% of companies offering training and 33% having a strategy in development.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 11, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 110}}], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': 'An aerial view of sunset over St Helier, with the ocean in the background.'}]}
